.TH "YAMLR-CATALOG" "1" "March 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
Yamlr validates your manifests against official Kubernetes JSON schemas. These schemas are distilled for performance and cached locally in \fB~/.Yamlr/catalogs\fR.
.PP
The \fByamlr catalog\fR command allows you to manage this local cache.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Check status of local catalog
yamlr catalog
.RE
.fi
.SS "Update Catalog"
Download the latest schemas from the upstream repository.
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr catalog update
.RE
.fi
.SS "List Versions"
See which Kubernetes versions are currently available in your local cache.
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr catalog list
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--kube-version V\fR**: Target version for catalog operations (alias: **\fB--k8s-version\fR**).
.SH "LAZY FETCHING"
As of Yamlr v1.0, you rarely need to run \fByamlr catalog update\fR manually.
.PP
If you run \fByamlr upgrade --to 1.32\fR and the v1.32 schema is missing, Yamlr will \fBautomatically download it\fR for you in the background.
.PP
